## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of modern CSS features: container queries, dense grid packing, aspect-ratio control, and CSS-only interactivity, plus accessibility considerations.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid with dense packing (grid-auto-flow: dense)
- Container Queries (@container) and container-type: inline-size on the grid
- aspect-ratio for consistent media areas
- Checkbox-based reveal (CSS-only) using :checked
- Staggered entrance via nth-child and animation delays
- prefers-reduced-motion and focus-visible accessibility

## Code Example
```css
.grid { container-type: inline-size; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 16px; grid-auto-flow: dense; }
@container (max-width: 1199px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
@container (max-width: 799px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.card { border:1px solid #ddd; border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; display:flex; flex-direction:column; animation: rise 400ms var(--stagger,0ms) both; }
.media { aspect-ratio:16/9; background:#ccc; }
.details { display:none; padding:8px; }
.card input:checked ~ .details { display:block; }
@keyframes rise { from { transform: translateY(8px); opacity:0; } to { transform: translateY(0); opacity:1; } }
.card { --stagger: 0ms; }
.card:nth-child(2){ --stagger: 40ms; }
.card:nth-child(3){ --stagger: 80ms; }
.card:nth-child(4){ --stagger: 120ms; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .card { animation: none; } }
```

